      "content": "I can help you draft a rejection email that's both professional and kind. Here's a sample:\n\n\"Dear [Candidate Name],\n\nI wanted to personally reach out to you regarding the status of your application for the Senior Developer position at [Company Name]. We were impressed by your exceptional technical skills and the time you took to showcase your expertise during the final round of interviews. Unfortunately, after careful consideration, we have decided to move forward with another candidate whose skills and experience best align with our current needs.\n\nPlease know that this decision was not made lightly, and we were truly impressed by your qualifications and passion for software development. Your dedication to your craft is evident, and I have no doubt that you will find a role that is an excellent fit for your skills and interests.\n\nWe appreciate the time and effort you invested in our hiring process, and we wish you the very best in your job search. If you have any questions or concerns, please don't hesitate to reach out.\n\nBest regards,\n[Your Name]\"\n\nI hope this helps! You can customize it to fit your company's tone and style. Remember, it's essential to be kind and professional, even when delivering bad news.",
